# Generated compiler and site output belongs to no language statistic and is
# hidden from diffs.
dist/** linguist-generated
examples/*/dist/** linguist-generated

# Eliscript is not yet listed in github-linguist's languages.yml, and Linguist
# ignores `linguist-language` for a language it does not know. Until an
# Eliscript entry merges, classify `.eli` sources as Lisp so the language bar
# and syntax highlighting show the Lisp-shaped source instead of unclassified
# text.
#
# To make GitHub report "Eliscript" with its own color, an entry must be added
# to `lib/linguist/languages.yml` with `type`, `color`, `extensions`,
# `tm_scope`, and `aliases`, together with a syntax-highlighting grammar added
# through `script/add-grammar`, representative samples under `samples/`, and a
# language id from `script/update-ids`. Linguist adds an extension only once it
# has sufficient in-the-wild usage. Once merged, delete the line below and let
# the real entry take effect.
*.eli linguist-language=Lisp
